# vvaharness/validation/config/overrides.py

The profile-sourced settings that seed the validation configuration. A profile sets only the keys it declares; every absent key falls back to the shipped default, never to the environment.

Source: `vvaharness/validation/config/overrides.py` (lines 1-49)
Executor: code
Called from: `vvaharness/validation/cli/_model.sudo` (builds it from the harness profile), `vvaharness/validation/config/settings/config.sudo` load_config (consumes it)

// src: vvaharness/validation/config/overrides.py:26-49
ValidateOverrides {   // every field optional ("total=False")
  model: String
  via: String
  provider: String | null
  use_responses_api: Boolean | null
  effort: EffortLevel
  max_turns: Number
  max_budget_usd: Number | null
  max_findings: Number | null
  timeout: Number
  max_model_calls: Number
  orchestrator_max_model_calls: Number
  security_architect_model: String
  penetration_tester_model: String
  cross_repo_analyzer_model: String
  validate_tools: String   // comma-separated tool allow-list for the reviewer personas
  cache_markers: Boolean
  // "the ``VVAHARNESS_*`` environment is never consulted for these (``_EnvScalars`` reads only its three credential/host-local scalars)"
}
